  "problem": "$\\frac{7}{10}\\times 6=$",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 6}{10}=\\frac{42}{10}\n$$\n\nWe then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{42}{10}=\\frac{42÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{21}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{21}{5}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n21÷5=4\\,\\text{R}1=4\\,\\frac{1}{5}\n$$",
